Subject: [PATCH] dmaengine: dma-jz4780: fix a NULL dereference in tx_status

terminate_all() clears jzchan->desc. A cyclic cookie never completes,
so a later tx_status() (ALSA calls it from sync_stop/hw_free when the
PCM is closed after a STOP, and from PREPARE after an XRUN) skips the
DMA_COMPLETE exit, does not find the descriptor on the issued list and
dereferences jzchan->desc:

  CPU 0 Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address 00000000
  epc in jz4780_dma_tx_status

With CONFIG_PANIC_ON_OOPS this reboots the SoC on every ALSA capture or
playback close after a start. Check jzchan->desc before using it.

Seen on a T31X (kernel 7.3.3, t31-aic capture).
---
--- a/drivers/dma/dma-jz4780.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/dma-jz4780.c
@@ -658,7 +658,7 @@
 		/* On the issued list, so hasn't been processed yet */
 		residue = jz4780_dma_desc_residue(jzchan,
 					to_jz4780_dma_desc(vdesc), 0);
-	} else if (cookie == jzchan->desc->vdesc.tx.cookie) {
+	} else if (jzchan->desc && cookie == jzchan->desc->vdesc.tx.cookie) {
 		residue = jz4780_dma_desc_residue(jzchan, jzchan->desc,
 					jzchan->curr_hwdesc + 1);
 	}
